#
# NOTHING IS SOURCED HERE.  A second copy of the packages would be two
# programs with one name: a renamed package once left its old binary and its
# old init script in an image beside the new ones, and two disk pack programs
# ran, each writing blocks back to the same file.  Packages have one home.
#
# The programs that run beside the CADR are Buildroot packages in the ARTY
# Z7-20's external tree, and there is one copy of them.  This board's build is
# given both trees:
#
#     BR2_EXTERNAL=boards/arty-z7-20/linux/buildroot:boards/kria-kr260/linux/buildroot
#
# and every `BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_*` symbol comes from the first.  What this tree
# adds is the board: the CADR's device tree over mainline's KR260 tree, the
# script the factory U-Boot runs from the card, the kernel's fragment and a
# defconfig.
